      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(codex): bound app-server websocket handshake waits at 30s",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where operators using Codex app-server over `websocket`/`unix` transport would hang forever on `initialize`/RPC when a peer accepted TCP but never completed the WebSocket upgrade. Pending frames never flush and the client never sees a transport exit, so the run cannot fail closed or reconnect.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- Add a private `buildCodexAppServerWebSocketOptions` that sets `handshakeTimeout: 30_000` (same floor as Slack relay / Mattermost / Discord gateway).\n- Both TCP and Unix upgrade paths consume that builder.\n- Guard `EventEmitter` error re-emit with `listenerCount` so callers that only wait on `exit` (handshake hang paths) are not disrupted by Node's unhandled-`error` throw.\n- Regressions observe production wiring in source (knip-safe) and prove stalled-handshake exit + `initialize` failure with a short test-only hang floor.\n\nNo new config/env surface.\n\n## User Impact\n\n**Before:** A Codex app-server endpoint that accepted TCP without completing the websocket handshake could pin `initialize`/RPC forever on that attempt.\n\n**After:** Handshake waits fail closed after 30s (`Opening handshake has timed out` → transport `exit` / client error), so the run can stop or recover instead of hanging.\n\n## Evidence\n\nHead: `ff774d4b812fbc925f7f13bfb4bcb4e08db940c2`\n\nExecutable negative control + fix proof:\n\n```bash\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/codex/src/app-server/transport-websocket.test.ts -- --run --reporter=verbose\n```\n\n```text\nstdout | extensions/codex/src/app-server/transport-websocket.test.ts > Codex app-server websocket transport > negative control: ws without handshakeTimeout stays CONNECTING on never-upgrade peer\n[codex handshake negative control] outcome=still-pending readyState=0 wait_ms=300 without_handshakeTimeout=true\n ✓ |extension-codex| extensions/codex/src/app-server/transport-websocket.test.ts > Codex app-server websocket transport > negative control: ws without handshakeTimeout stays CONNECTING on never-upgrade peer 306ms\n[codex handshake proof] timed_out=true elapsed_ms=200 code=1006 handshakeTimeout_ms=200 production_ms=30000\n    187|       `[codex handshake negative control] outcome=${outcome} readyStat…\nThe latest test that might've caused the error is \"negative control: ws without handshakeTimeout stays CONNECTING on never-upgrade peer\". It might mean one of the following:\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  6 passed (6)\n```\n\n- **Negative control (executable):** plain `ws.WebSocket` with **no** `handshakeTimeout` against the same TCP-accept / never-upgrade fixture stays `CONNECTING` / `still-pending` after 300ms.\n- **After fix:** `createWebSocketTransport` with `handshakeTimeoutMs: 200` emits `exit` (~200ms); production wiring asserts `CODEX_APP_SERVER_WS_HANDSHAKE_TIMEOUT_MS = 30_000` in the private builder.\n- Touched: `extensions/codex/src/app-server/transport-websocket.ts` (+ colocated test). Sibling Slack relay / Mattermost / Discord handshake floors unchanged.\n\nAI-assisted.\n",
        "branch": "fix/codex-app-server-ws-handshake-timeout",
